If you know how to fix this error in anaconda sources, even if this is
hack applicable only in your particular case, then you are likely
interested in an information on this page:
http://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Anaconda/Updates

What is missing there is that if you are doing "Updates from the Tree"
then updates.img is a gzipped cpio archive, created with "-H newc"
option, with replacement Python source files and anaconda will load that
automatically if only present.  You do not need the whole anaconda;
only those files you want to modify.

