Hello Oliver, 

	Not yet, due to lack of infrastructure.


Only thing we got, is a good place where publish packages and releases, thats all.

    We use a simple method, and we only keep 'touched' packages in an SRPMS folder, 
so all alpha specific patches are embeded in src.rpms:

e.g for 3.0b branch
ftp://ftp.rdsor.ro/pub/Linux/Distributions/AlphaLinux/core/3.0b/SRPMS

    We dont keep any other src.rpm , they are aviable on fedora mirrors, and those unlisted
packs are the same as ours, i see no sense republish tham too.
   We olso tag 'axp' string over packages to show up that it contain specific alpha hooks,
and package differ from original fedora one.

