As an aside from Cristian's comments - I'm currently looking at use  
either CVS or SVN for checking in my "extras" packages, and possibly  
updates. There are a lot of tools out there that have been developed  
to make repository and package management easier, and I'm exploring  
them.

If anyone would _like_ CVS or SVN space for anything Alpha-related, I  
can provide it quite easily. Email me off-list and we can talk about it.



Also, if anyone's been particularly observant, you may have noticed  
the first package update has appeared for AC3, mainly as a result of  
testing the build environment.

Updates will be signed with this key: http://ftp.alphacore.info/alpha/ 
core/3/os/RPM-GPG-KEY-ac-updates

The first update is the avahi packages. It's complex enough to show  
up issues in the build system, and (probably) not so mission-critical  
to anyone that breakage will render anything unusable. Please  
consider enabling the updates repository in your yum config, and  
letting me know if there are issues with the process.



